  "diagnosis_text": "Confirmed: **h1 \u2192 h5 ICMP fails completely** (3/3 packets lost).\n\nThe fault is localized to the configured inter-switch link **s3 port 1 \u2194 s4 port 2**:\n\n- ONOS no longer reports that link in the active topology (only 4 of the expected 5 ring links are active).\n- `s3-eth1` is **disabled**.\n- `s4-eth2` is **disabled**.\n- The other ring links, including the direct alternate path `s1 \u2194 s5`, are reported active.\n\nSo this is a **link/port-down condition between s3 and s4**, not a host-facing port fault on h1 or h5. The h1-to-h5 outage despite the surviving s1\u2013s5 link indicates forwarding has not provided a working alternate path (or has not converged), but the directly observable physical/localized fault is the **s3\u2013s4 inter-switch connection**.\n\nNext action: restore or administratively enable the `s3-eth1` / `s4-eth2` link, then verify ONOS rediscovers it and retest h1\u2192h5.",
